{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-ui-settings-002-01", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/TooltipEchoBudgetTests.cs", "line": 151, "method": "LiteralGuiContentTooltips_FitTheHelpStrip", "category": "T4", "severity": "Medium", "confidence": "medium", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek.Tests/TooltipEchoBudgetTests.cs:407 (sut=wiring-gate); ExtractLiteralGuiContentTooltips scans raw source without StripLineComments, so commenting out one live `new GUIContent(label, tooltip)` in UI/TimelineWindowUI.cs (floor 14, margin 0) still counts it -> stays green", "what_it_asserts": "Every literal GUIContent tooltip in each strip-hosting window is newline-free and within that window's char budget, and that at least minTooltips of them were found.", "why_weak": "ExtractLiteralGuiContentTooltips (line 407) searches the raw file text; StripLineComments is applied only inside TryDecodeLiteralRun and in ExtractTooltipEchoBoxLineArgs (line 679). A commented-out GUIContent therefore counts toward the floor, so on the margin-0 rows (UI/TimelineWindowUI.cs floor 14, ParsekUI.cs floor 8) a real tooltip can be removed or commented out with the anti-vacuity floor still satisfied - the fail-GREEN direction the floor exists to prevent. SortableHeaderTooltips_FitTheRecordingsStrip (line 296, floor 6) scans raw source the same way.", "proposed_action": "Run the source through StripLineComments once at the top of ExtractLiteralGuiContentTooltips and of the DrawSortableHeader scan (both already have the helper in-file), so commented-out call sites neither count toward the floor nor get budgeted.", "effort": "M", "july_ref": "none"}
{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-ui-settings-002-02", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/TimelineWindowUITests.cs", "line": 85, "method": "ShouldShowFastForwardButton_FutureRecording_ReturnsTrue", "category": "T3", "severity": "Medium", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/UI/TimelineWindowUI.cs:1590; stub ShouldShowFastForwardButton to `return true;` -> still green; only `return false;` -> red", "what_it_asserts": "ShouldShowFastForwardButton returns true for a non-null recording on a future row.", "why_weak": "The SUT is `isFuture && rec != null` and only the all-true input is pinned; neither the isFuture=false nor the rec=null half is asserted anywhere directly, so a body that ignores both arguments passes. Its sibling ShouldShowWatchButton has both cases (lines 142 and 149).", "proposed_action": "Add the two negative cases (isFuture:false and rec:null) beside it, mirroring ShouldShowWatchButton_NonFlightRecording_ReturnsFalse.", "effort": "S", "july_ref": "none"}
